WEBVTT

00:03.149 --> 00:06.443
Because you're going to join me.

00:07.404 --> 00:11.904
I'll defeat your boss and
take back this town.

00:13.535 --> 00:14.369
What?!

00:14.744 --> 00:18.122
To remove the child-exploiting,
drug-dealing mafiosi,

00:18.248 --> 00:21.459
I must become a mafioso.

00:21.584 --> 00:22.960
Are you saying…

00:23.253 --> 00:26.047
you want to join our syndicate?!

00:26.214 --> 00:27.548
Are you mad?!

00:27.674 --> 00:28.883
Do you know what
that would entail?

00:28.925 --> 00:31.052
- Do you know what you're saying?!
- Beautiful, isn't it?

00:32.470 --> 00:34.972
Yes. If I'm going to
take back this town,

00:35.098 --> 00:37.058
then I'll have to join
the syndicate that controls it

00:37.100 --> 00:38.684
and work my way up to the top.

00:39.394 --> 00:40.395
Bucciarati,

00:40.937 --> 00:43.689
I will become a Primo Mafioso!

00:45.275 --> 00:46.484
Pass! Pass!

00:56.077 --> 00:56.827
Grazie!

00:56.870 --> 00:57.745
- Grazie.
- Grazie Mille!

00:58.288 --> 00:59.330
Fine then.

00:59.831 --> 01:03.000
I'll report I was unable to
locate Luca's attacker

01:03.084 --> 01:06.045
and will introduce you to begin
the initiation process.

01:06.463 --> 01:10.963
But if it gets out that you're
trying to take down the boss…

01:11.926 --> 01:13.594
you're on your own.

01:13.928 --> 01:16.972
A traitor stands alone,
an island of isolation.

01:17.640 --> 01:20.267
Your failure will be yours
and yours alone.

01:24.230 --> 01:26.148
Nothing is certain,
but your noble resolve,

01:26.191 --> 01:27.817
even at the cost of
self mutilation,

01:27.859 --> 01:32.280
and your golden aspirations
command respect and my support…

01:32.655 --> 01:34.031
Giorno Giovanna.

01:46.586 --> 01:51.086
<i>Heavy stones of fate
are holding down my dreams</i>

01:51.925 --> 01:55.386
<i>It feels as if I'm being crushed</i>

01:57.180 --> 02:01.680
<i>I've been staggering around
with nowhere to hide</i>

02:02.352 --> 02:06.189
<i>But I will never give in</i>

02:06.231 --> 02:10.731
<i>I know there are fragments of hope
buried beneath all that rubble</i>

02:18.034 --> 02:22.534
<i>I will find them with my own hands
and turn this world upside down</i>

02:31.089 --> 02:35.589
<i>Fighting gold
We will shine one day</i>

02:37.053 --> 02:41.553
<i>As long as we continue to
believe in our own path</i>

02:44.143 --> 02:47.271
<i>We are unyielding souls</i>

02:47.355 --> 02:51.855
<i>Our battle against god
will keep raging on</i>

02:52.569 --> 02:57.069
<i>Until our final days
Fighting gold</i>

03:06.791 --> 03:11.291
EPISODE 03
MEET THE MAFIOSO BEHIND THE WALL

03:09.335 --> 03:12.234
Our famiglia controls
all business in Napoli.

03:14.424 --> 03:17.260
Passione… That is the name
of our group.

03:17.760 --> 03:22.260
Passione might be a fitting moniker,
but understand it's not the boss's name.

03:22.765 --> 03:25.225
No one knows his name,

03:25.268 --> 03:27.144
and no one has
any idea what he looks like.

03:27.645 --> 03:30.522
Orders are passed down via
a multitude of capos.

03:31.024 --> 03:34.652
Giorno, the capo who will decide
your future in the famiglia

03:34.777 --> 03:36.153
is a man named Polpo.

03:37.238 --> 03:40.241
He resides in this building.

03:41.284 --> 03:42.535
But this is…

03:42.702 --> 03:45.496
LOOM

03:43.828 --> 03:45.496
This is a prison.

03:45.872 --> 03:48.791
Esatto. Polpo was convicted
and sentenced

03:48.833 --> 03:50.459
to fifteen years in prison.

03:51.127 --> 03:53.838
He issues my orders and
manages all aspects of the famiglia

03:53.921 --> 03:56.006
from within those walls.

03:56.382 --> 03:59.385
He can leave whenever
the desire strikes him,

03:59.469 --> 04:00.970
but he chooses not to.

04:01.471 --> 04:03.181
He simply has no need.

04:03.222 --> 04:04.223
Perche?

04:04.307 --> 04:05.933
You'll have your answer inside.

04:06.100 --> 04:07.142
Giorno Giovanna,

04:07.185 --> 04:10.021
in a matter of minutes,
he will conduct your interview.

04:10.063 --> 04:11.522
You must pass.

04:11.939 --> 04:14.024
It's no different from
an ordinary interview.

04:14.025 --> 04:16.944
His mood will dictate its content.

04:17.403 --> 04:20.030
And remember…
He must never find out.

04:21.324 --> 04:22.450
I understand.

04:24.160 --> 04:26.537
Before I forget…
You mentioned Stands…

04:26.913 --> 04:28.247
I believe, yes?

04:28.414 --> 04:32.459
I never asked…
How did you acquire yours?

04:32.919 --> 04:34.420
Are there others?

04:34.462 --> 04:36.547
Again, you'll have
your answer inside…

04:36.964 --> 04:38.382
If you pass.

04:42.595 --> 04:44.513
All right, I need your watch

04:44.555 --> 04:47.140
and everything in your pockets
on this tray.

04:47.266 --> 04:50.310
Then you can move on
to the pat-down.

05:06.119 --> 05:09.205
Stand right there,
hands over your head.

05:10.873 --> 05:15.252
Go through the gate,
and continue down the hall.

05:15.920 --> 05:19.632
N-28 is Polpo's cell.

05:20.216 --> 05:24.220
Reinforced glass keeps him in his cell,
but you can still converse.

05:24.303 --> 05:27.139
Exchanging objects,

05:27.223 --> 05:30.309
either from him or yourself,
is strictly forbidden.

05:31.227 --> 05:33.229
You have fifteen minutes.

05:35.064 --> 05:38.358
I'll close the gate behind you.

05:38.443 --> 05:40.528
If he tries anything, just yell.

05:40.945 --> 05:43.405
I'm talking to him while
he's in his cell?

05:43.614 --> 05:44.948
There's no dedicated room?

05:45.032 --> 05:48.076
You don't know who he is?

06:17.231 --> 06:19.149
It's injured, isn't it?

06:19.609 --> 06:21.110
Your left arm.

06:28.618 --> 06:31.203
<i>That's… not a bed</i>

06:31.370 --> 06:33.246
GWOOO

06:33.664 --> 06:36.208
Isolated to the fingers of
your right hand,

06:36.292 --> 06:38.502
a faint yet distinct red marking
stretches before my eyes,

06:38.586 --> 06:40.504
as if you were gripping something.

06:40.588 --> 06:43.007
They're the markings
left behind by a bag.

06:43.216 --> 06:46.052
Which means,
you have been carrying a bag

06:46.135 --> 06:48.178
in exclusively your right hand.

06:48.471 --> 06:50.055
Now why would that be?

06:50.139 --> 06:52.683
Well, um… You'd be correct.

06:53.142 --> 06:55.352
I was using my right hand
to carry my bag.

06:55.478 --> 06:58.189
And indeed, I injured my left arm.

07:02.068 --> 07:03.694
Oh, to be young
and reckless again…

07:03.736 --> 07:06.029
What I would give to
have a body like yours.

07:08.241 --> 07:09.909
Do you drink wine?

07:10.493 --> 07:13.162
This Chianti Classico
is motto bene.

07:13.329 --> 07:17.041
Pair it with a bit of cracker,
scamorzza, and caviar,

07:17.083 --> 07:18.876
and you have perfection.

07:18.960 --> 07:21.504
They told me I'm not allowed
to give you anything,

07:21.546 --> 07:24.090
and that I can't accept anything
from you either.

07:25.633 --> 07:27.509
That's just a formality.

07:27.510 --> 07:31.597
What people say and what people do…

07:33.683 --> 07:36.394
are two different things.

07:36.519 --> 07:40.898
Therein lies the flaw
and the virtue, yes…

07:41.274 --> 07:45.774
I suppose the only real tragedy to
being holed up in this cell is… well…

07:47.196 --> 07:48.405
<i>- Polpo…</i>
- That I am no longer able to gaze up

07:48.489 --> 07:49.448
in admiration at the treasure

07:49.448 --> 07:52.367
<i>- So what if he doesn't have to leave the prison?</i>
- that is Michelangelo's Sistine Chapel ceiling.

07:52.660 --> 07:54.995
<i>It wouldn't matter
if he left or stayed</i>

07:55.746 --> 08:00.083
<i>With that carcass…
he's probably safer in there.</i>

08:00.543 --> 08:05.043
<i>But even more bizarre,
how'd he fit through the door?</i>

08:05.172 --> 08:08.008
Bucciarati's told me
all about you.

08:10.219 --> 08:12.763
So you want to be
a part of our famiglia?

08:12.847 --> 08:15.891
Hmm… Giorno Giovanna, was it?

08:16.225 --> 08:20.725
Well, I suppose we should commence
the interview, yes?

08:39.248 --> 08:40.749
<i>What was that?</i>

08:40.791 --> 08:42.042
<i>Am I hallucinating?</i>

08:42.585 --> 08:45.963
<i>For a second, it looked like
he was munching away on his fingers…</i>

08:46.380 --> 08:50.880
<i>Or… maybe this cazzone Polpo is just
another Stand user like Bucciarati.</i>

08:53.387 --> 08:57.474
<i>Either way, I can't let him
find out about me.</i>

08:58.100 --> 09:00.769
In separating the wheat
from the chaff,

09:00.811 --> 09:05.311
what do you think is of utmost importance,
Giorno Giovanna?

09:07.568 --> 09:10.153
You have to think of what
a person can do… right?

09:10.237 --> 09:13.990
Oh? Then what can you do, ragazzo?

09:18.454 --> 09:22.166
I grabbed a few souvenirs during
my pat-down back there.

09:22.500 --> 09:25.169
I thought they might come in handy
during our little test.

09:25.711 --> 09:27.921
Of course, I'll return them
on my way out.

09:32.593 --> 09:34.344
Is that all you have to show me?

09:34.428 --> 09:37.973
Besides that,
the only trick I can do is…

09:38.224 --> 09:40.726
fold my ear neatly into
my ear canal.

09:44.313 --> 09:46.523
Ah, motto interesante…

09:47.692 --> 09:48.609
But, you see…

09:49.694 --> 09:53.406
There's something very important
we haven't discussed,

09:53.823 --> 09:57.660
and that's trust, Giorno Giovanna.

09:58.160 --> 10:02.660
The most important quality
in selecting an associate is trust.

10:03.791 --> 10:08.291
By comparison,
intelligence and talent are

10:08.337 --> 10:11.715
no more significant than the piece
of cracker stuck between my teeth.

10:13.384 --> 10:17.388
My test will tell me exactly
how trustworthy you are.

10:17.638 --> 10:20.223
The flame of this lighter
reveals all.

10:23.227 --> 10:27.272
Take it and go forth.
Do not let the flame expire.

10:30.860 --> 10:32.236
Aspetta.

10:32.361 --> 10:35.030
I warn you you must exercise
great caution.

10:35.448 --> 10:38.576
The seventeenth-century
theologian Fuller once said,

10:39.035 --> 10:43.535
"He's my friend that
speaks well of me behind my back."

10:44.790 --> 10:46.917
If you want to become
a part of our famiglia,

10:46.959 --> 10:49.169
you will need to demonstrate
your trustworthiness

10:49.211 --> 10:51.129
even when no one is looking.

10:51.547 --> 10:53.298
For the next 24 hours,

10:53.382 --> 10:57.803
you must maintain possession of
that lighter without it extinguishing.

10:59.388 --> 11:03.308
If you are successful,
I will welcome you into our famiglia.

11:03.392 --> 11:04.810
Straightforward, yes?

11:04.894 --> 11:07.271
Don't worry,
there's plenty of fluid.

11:08.022 --> 11:11.483
Sit patiently in your room
until 3 p.m. tomorrow

11:11.567 --> 11:14.111
looking after that flame,
and we're a posto.

11:14.487 --> 11:18.073
If you are a man of
prudence and perseverance,

11:18.199 --> 11:19.783
nothing should happen
to that light.

11:20.117 --> 11:23.453
And you will have proven
your trustworthiness.

11:23.746 --> 11:25.748
However…

11:26.040 --> 11:29.793
If you happen to be the kind of man
who takes what I have to say lightly,

11:29.835 --> 11:33.797
say you nod off, sneeze,
or stumble,

11:33.839 --> 11:37.259
or a gust of wind extinguishes
that precious flame…

11:39.095 --> 11:43.349
I will know you cannot be trusted,

11:43.432 --> 11:45.600
I will know you are not part
of our famiglia.

11:46.018 --> 11:49.187
Now, take thee thy light
and go forth.

11:49.688 --> 11:52.065
Behold, the key to our famiglia.

11:59.782 --> 12:02.326
You have 24 hours.

12:02.743 --> 12:07.243
I look forward to our second meeting
tomorrow at 3 p.m.

12:09.208 --> 12:10.834
<i>24 hours…</i>

12:11.293 --> 12:15.171
All visitors must proceed through
the gate for a final pat-down.

12:18.843 --> 12:21.136
Once we give you permission
to exit the premises,

12:21.470 --> 12:24.639
you may proceed to the next room
to retrieve your belongings.

12:24.974 --> 12:28.060
Wait! Polpo has said
nothing to you?

12:28.394 --> 12:29.269
What?

12:31.272 --> 12:32.564
Your body search starts now.

12:32.731 --> 12:34.023
This is your last warning,

12:34.066 --> 12:37.152
accepting anything from a convict
is punishable by law!

12:37.194 --> 12:40.697
<i>Merda… I was sure
he would've bribed these cops</i>

12:40.781 --> 12:43.116
<i>to let me walk out of here
with that lighter!</i>

12:43.200 --> 12:44.326
Attenzione…

12:44.368 --> 12:46.703
Put your hands above your head
and step forward now!

12:46.996 --> 12:50.708
<i>So Polpo's test has
already started…</i>

12:50.791 --> 12:51.541
<i>And…</i>

12:52.168 --> 12:55.171
<i>That means there's no turning back!
I have to pass…</i>

12:55.212 --> 12:56.379
<i>I don't care what it takes,</i>

12:56.505 --> 12:59.299
<i>I have to become part of
the Passione famiglia!</i>

13:03.512 --> 13:05.555
KOICHI HIROSE
REVERB ACT 3

13:06.015 --> 13:08.017
I already told you, step forward!

13:08.142 --> 13:09.434
<i>- I was able to conceal…</i>
- Hands in the air,

13:09.518 --> 13:11.728
<i>- in the palm of my hand</i>
- come forward now!

13:11.770 --> 13:12.729
I will perform a search!

13:12.813 --> 13:14.105
<i>I can hide this flame!</i>

13:44.887 --> 13:46.179
You're okay.

13:46.555 --> 13:48.139
I see no reason to not let you go.

13:48.682 --> 13:50.642
I give you permission to
exit the premises.

13:50.726 --> 13:51.601
However…

13:51.644 --> 13:54.104
I ask that you show me
your palms first.

13:54.939 --> 13:56.899
I'll say it one more time,

13:56.941 --> 13:59.944
you are prohibited by law to
accept any objects from a convict.

14:00.194 --> 14:03.780
Now open your hands!
That's an order.

14:16.627 --> 14:17.628
A flower?

14:20.589 --> 14:22.215
An actual flower?

14:23.300 --> 14:27.304
Fine. If that's the worst you got.

14:27.388 --> 14:29.223
Our visitor is free to go.

14:37.690 --> 14:39.316
I transformed the lighter
into a flower

14:39.358 --> 14:41.651
and hid the flame itself
within the petals.

14:42.278 --> 14:43.862
That was too close.

14:44.405 --> 14:48.905
Could the flame be part
of Polpo's Stand?

15:00.546 --> 15:02.506
<i>The wind is a major problem!</i>

15:02.548 --> 15:04.591
Hey, Giorno! Perfect timing!

15:04.967 --> 15:07.511
Could you be a pal and press
the shutter button for us?

15:07.636 --> 15:08.470
Not a chance.

15:11.265 --> 15:14.017
Sousa mi, would you mind
lending me a hand?

15:14.310 --> 15:15.060
Not now.

15:23.694 --> 15:26.196
<i>Finally made it back to
the dorm safe and sound</i>

15:32.995 --> 15:34.788
Th-That was close…

15:44.381 --> 15:47.634
This should keep it upright,
and even if there's a little draft,

15:47.760 --> 15:49.720
it shouldn't be enough
to blow out the light.

15:50.095 --> 15:52.514
Now, just as Polpo said,
all I have to do

15:52.556 --> 15:56.893
is remain diligent and watch this flame
with my life for the next 23 hours.

15:57.519 --> 15:58.645
Of course.

15:58.854 --> 16:01.648
I have to make sure the window
is good and locked.

16:02.316 --> 16:05.235
Never know when a gust of wind
could strike.

16:09.948 --> 16:11.199
<i>What?</i>

16:11.241 --> 16:13.451
<i>Who would just go
and open my door?</i>

16:15.245 --> 16:16.913
<i>Th-That's—</i>

16:20.125 --> 16:21.876
He must be out.

16:22.461 --> 16:23.712
Well, it's now or never.

16:24.171 --> 16:26.006
<i>It's the Japanese tourist again!</i>

16:26.090 --> 16:28.592
<i>There's no question…
that's Koichi Hirose!</i>

16:29.051 --> 16:31.678
<i>How could he know
where I live?</i>

16:33.597 --> 16:35.015
Looks like he did something
with my suitcase

16:35.057 --> 16:36.933
and everything that was inside.

16:37.017 --> 16:41.062
But my passport might
still be around.

16:41.271 --> 16:45.771
Selling off that kind of personal ID's
got to be a little more involved.

16:46.235 --> 16:48.570
I can't believe
I'm sneaking into someone's room…

16:48.612 --> 16:50.155
I look like a thief, but…

16:50.364 --> 16:52.491
No! What am I saying?!
He's the thief!

16:52.658 --> 16:55.077
All I'm doing is looking for
what belongs to me!

16:55.411 --> 16:57.579
<i>His passport… Ah, cazzo!</i>

16:58.038 --> 17:00.623
<i>It's in the box on my desk…</i>

17:00.833 --> 17:02.459
<i>I was going to give it back to him!</i>

17:02.543 --> 17:05.963
<i>It's just a matter of time…
Koichi will find that flame!</i>

17:06.046 --> 17:08.798
<i>There's no question,
he'll put it out!</i>

17:09.091 --> 17:10.759
<i>He'll just think
it's a fire hazard!</i>

17:11.468 --> 17:13.178
<i>Dammit, think… think.</i>

17:13.262 --> 17:16.473
<i>I've got to get that lighter
back in my hands!</i>

17:18.600 --> 17:20.393
<i>Golden Wind!</i>

17:31.113 --> 17:35.575
<i>Golden Wind managed to turn
that cord into a snake.</i>

17:35.826 --> 17:37.619
<i>I knew you'd like that bread</i>

17:38.120 --> 17:39.412
<i>Bravo… Nice job digging in!</i>

17:40.080 --> 17:41.831
<i>Now to reel it in with the cord…</i>

17:42.666 --> 17:44.334
<i>What? Shit!</i>

17:50.215 --> 17:51.507
<i>I can't believe it.</i>

17:51.633 --> 17:53.343
<i>He still found the lighter.</i>

17:53.802 --> 17:55.136
<i>Shit, everything's going to hell.</i>

17:55.637 --> 17:58.723
<i>I just need to make sure
he doesn't blow it out!</i>

17:59.308 --> 18:00.183
Oh?

18:02.436 --> 18:05.939
That's the imperial seal!
That's the national seal of Japan!

18:05.981 --> 18:09.359
Got it! I found my passport!

18:10.694 --> 18:12.529
I-It's on fire!

18:16.158 --> 18:17.450
Thank goodness…

18:18.452 --> 18:19.369
Huh?

18:19.703 --> 18:23.289
Well, that's weird…
I know I saw a lit lighter…

18:25.083 --> 18:26.167
Another close one.

18:26.919 --> 18:29.504
He almost put out that flame.

18:30.297 --> 18:32.882
No one is going to extinguish
my dream!

18:33.300 --> 18:35.468
And the first step to
realizing my goal

18:35.511 --> 18:38.055
is protecting this flame
with my life!

18:41.934 --> 18:43.143
Oh, just missed you there.

18:43.227 --> 18:47.022
Very sorry. I was trying to
clean the stairs.

18:47.105 --> 18:51.605
Glad I just misted you there.
Almost gave you a shower.

18:52.402 --> 18:56.739
I suppose we've both done our fair share
of good deeds then, right?

18:57.199 --> 18:59.826
Living each day as the good lord
intended is very important.

18:59.910 --> 19:04.410
Had you not, there's no question
you would be soaking wet right now.

19:06.583 --> 19:09.544
Porca miseria. I don't believe it.

19:10.003 --> 19:10.878
The flame…

19:11.755 --> 19:15.550
<i>Maybe I can beg Polpo to
let me just start over.</i>

19:16.385 --> 19:17.427
<i>I can't…</i>

19:17.886 --> 19:19.470
<i>If he were that forgiving,</i>

19:19.555 --> 19:22.182
<i>he wouldn't be putting me
through this test.</i>

19:22.432 --> 19:23.641
Flame?

19:23.725 --> 19:27.186
My goodness, is that lighter
refusing to turn on?

19:27.729 --> 19:31.149
I hope I didn't break it.
You sure it won't work?

19:31.233 --> 19:33.443
Sorry, this doesn't concern you.

19:33.735 --> 19:36.446
I'm just trying to figure out
what I should do next…

19:36.572 --> 19:40.867
From the looks of it,
it might still be in working order.

19:41.118 --> 19:44.996
I think I hear it releasing fuel.

19:45.080 --> 19:47.248
What did you just say?

19:48.667 --> 19:50.585
WHOOSH

19:50.877 --> 19:53.379
I was right.
Something's definitely coming out.

19:53.422 --> 19:55.298
This must be how
you switch it on…

19:55.549 --> 19:56.800
Did you try here?

19:57.259 --> 19:59.135
That'd be impossible.

19:59.261 --> 20:02.097
- Why would you be able to turn it back on?
- What a beautiful design!

20:02.097 --> 20:03.932
It's either on or it's not.

20:03.932 --> 20:05.475
- That's the test.
- You don't see craftsmanship…

20:05.475 --> 20:07.059
- If I could just reignite the thing,
- like this anymore.

20:07.060 --> 20:08.978
What would be the point
of the test?!

20:11.982 --> 20:14.526
Granted, that was more a blowtorch
than a lighter,

20:14.568 --> 20:18.405
but I think I got it working again.

20:18.905 --> 20:19.655
See?

20:19.823 --> 20:24.323
Now, I see you're carrying a lighter,
but you're not a smoker, are you?

20:26.788 --> 20:27.997
<i>Something's wrong.</i>

20:28.123 --> 20:31.042
<i>It reignited…
Something has to be wrong!</i>

20:41.094 --> 20:42.095
<i>What the—?!</i>

20:42.596 --> 20:44.848
<i>That couldn't be his Sta–</i>

20:45.015 --> 20:47.851
It was you…
You reignited the flame.

20:48.477 --> 20:52.731
I offer you salvation.
Before you lie two paths.

20:53.148 --> 20:54.274
Th-That's…

20:54.650 --> 20:58.111
Do you live and become
one of the chosen…

20:58.320 --> 21:01.197
or do you proceed along
the path of death?

21:01.782 --> 21:02.949
<i>A Stand!</i>

21:02.991 --> 21:05.410
<i>This is Polpo's Stand!</i>

21:05.577 --> 21:06.786
<i>It's clear as day!</i>

21:06.828 --> 21:09.497
You are the one
who reignited the flame!

21:09.873 --> 21:11.833
You shall receive my arrow!

21:13.543 --> 21:16.712
That's too far, bastardo!
You've messed with the wrong kid!

21:21.301 --> 21:22.802
This soul…

21:23.512 --> 21:27.140
is not the soul of the chosen.

21:27.516 --> 21:29.267
<i>The soul of the chosen?</i>

21:32.813 --> 21:34.314
H-Hey, are you…?

21:35.774 --> 21:38.902
<i>Emorto. There's no wound,
but he's dead…</i>

21:39.277 --> 21:42.488
<i>The arrow definitely pierced him,
but was it his soul…?</i>

21:42.989 --> 21:45.825
<i>So he rips a person's soul
from their body</i>

21:45.867 --> 21:47.910
<i>and ends their life with
a pierce from the arrow?</i>

21:47.994 --> 21:49.578
<i>Is that how he does it?</i>

21:49.955 --> 21:53.458
<i>But the soul of the chosen…</i>

21:53.959 --> 21:56.711
<i>Is that someone who gets to be
part of the famiglia?</i>

21:57.212 --> 21:59.214
You, too, have reignited the flame.

21:59.256 --> 22:03.756
I offer you salvation.
Before you lies two paths…

23:38.146 --> 23:42.108
EPISODE 04
JOINING THE FAMIGLIA
